  "critique": {
    "acceptable": false,
    "blocking_issues": [
      "The mapping emits BN_ABN as entity.abn without an explicit exact-membership filter for this field. The documentation says BN_ABN can be NULL when an ABN was issued by a previous regulator and not recorded with ASIC, when multiple ABNs exist, or when suppressed; however, a populated value is explicitly described as an ABN. The supplied engine semantics make the ABN transform checksum-validating, so this is semantically defensible only for valid values, but the mapping does not establish that the ABN identifies the legal entity or holder. Given the ontology's entity.abn meaning and the declared subject grain business_name_holder, emitting it as a legal-entity attribute risks asserting ownership/linkage that the source does not prove.",
      "The mapping emits BN_NAME as entity.trading_name while its subject is a business-name registration, not a legal entity. This is a reasonable partial representation, but the target entity field requires an entity interpretation and the mapping does not define a separate business-name subject/object or a deterministic legal-entity link. It therefore risks presenting the registered business name as a trading name of a canonical entity rather than preserving it solely as a source business-name observation."
    ],
    "warnings": [
